abstract: >-
  A web-based assessment platform for measuring financial literacy among
  university students using a pre-post research design with adaptive
  diagnostic follow-up (SDM-10). The platform administers a 40-item anchor
  assessment across three knowledge domains (Borrowing and Credit, Behavioral
  and Risk Management, Investment and Risk-Return) followed by a 10-item
  adaptive diagnostic module that targets individual knowledge gaps. Developed
  for QUINN 102 (Financial Literacy) at Loyola University Chicago, Spring 2026.
  Pre-course baseline: N=421 completers (97.2% completion rate), M=66.55%,
  SD=17.38%.
